  Sign in from the Slack desktop app

  The Slack app on this Mac is signed in to these workspaces:

   ✓ Acme Corp                                                 acme.slack.com
     Acme Corp                                              acme-eu.slack.com
   ✓ Gamma                                                    gamma.slack.com

  When macOS asks about "Slack Safe Storage", press Allow, not Always Allow.

  Enter to sign in, Space to mark several, j/k or Up/Down to choose, p to
  paste a browser request (Cmd+V pastes one you copied already).

  The prompt names "security", the system tool slakio reads the key with.
  Always Allow would let any program read that key without asking. slakio
  reads the Slack app's files and changes nothing; the sign-in goes to the
  macOS Keychain.

  Ctrl+Q  Quit
  ?       Keyboard help


 NORMAL               │ Enter sign in · j/k choose · p paste a request · ? help
